{"title":"Career roadmap — Formulation Assistant","role":"Formulation Assistant","summary":"A Formulation Assistant supports the development, testing, optimisation, and scale-up of chemical or polymer-based formulations. Depending on the industry, this can include coatings, adhesives, plastics, rubber, inks, paints, construction chemicals, cosmetics, pharmaceuticals, specialty chemicals, and advanced materials.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Polymer Science / Industrial Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role is particularly suitable for someone who combines chemistry fundamentals + polymer science + laboratory testing + formulation experimentation + quality control."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What to build","Likely opportunities"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Chemistry, polymers, formulation, laboratory techniques"},{"text":"Formulation Assistant, QC Chemist, R&D Assistant"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Formulation optimisation, DOE, analytical instruments, scale-up"},{"text":"Formulation Chemist, R&D Executive, Process Development Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Product development, technical leadership, advanced materials"},{"text":"Senior Formulation Scientist, R&D Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Innovation, sustainable materials, AI-assisted formulation, leadership"},{"text":"Principal Scientist, Technical Manager, R&D Head"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build during the B.Sc.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Chemistry foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"General chemistry"},{"text":"Organic chemistry"},{"text":"Inorganic chemistry"},{"text":"Physical chemistry"},{"text":"Analytical chemistry"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Chemical bonding"},{"text":"Reaction mechanisms"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical laboratory skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accurate weighing"},{"text":"Solution preparation"},{"text":"Titration"},{"text":"pH measurement"},{"text":"Filtration"},{"text":"Centrifugation"},{"text":"Heating/cooling operations"},{"text":"Basic spectroscopy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Polymer and industrial chemistry"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polymer chemistry"},{"text":"Polymerisation mechanisms"},{"text":"Addition and condensation polymerisation"},{"text":"Copolymers"},{"text":"Molecular weight"},{"text":"Glass-transition temperature"},{"text":"Crystallinity"},{"text":"Rheology"},{"text":"Polymer degradation"},{"text":"Polymer additives"},{"text":"Industrial chemistry"},{"text":"Surface chemistry"},{"text":"Colloid chemistry"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand major formulation components:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Resins"},{"text":"Binders"},{"text":"Solvents"},{"text":"Plasticisers"},{"text":"Surfactants"},{"text":"Dispersants"},{"text":"Pigments"},{"text":"Fillers"},{"text":"Stabilizers"},{"text":"Catalysts"},{"text":"Curing agents"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Formulation and product development"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the complete formulation cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw materials","formulation design","mixing","testing","optimisation","stability","scale-up","quality evaluation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Formulation preparation"},{"text":"Mixing and dispersion"},{"text":"Viscosity measurement"},{"text":"pH adjustment"},{"text":"Density measurement"},{"text":"Particle-size analysis"},{"text":"Stability testing"},{"text":"Compatibility testing"},{"text":"Rheological testing"},{"text":"Thermal analysis"},{"text":"Colour measurement"},{"text":"Adhesion testing"},{"text":"Hardness testing"},{"text":"Tensile testing"}]},{"t